# ============================================================
# PROJECT RULES — TREASURE DIGITAL
# Premium bilingual (BG default, EN) digital agency website.
# Cursor: follow these rules on EVERY edit and generation.
# Source of truth for full detail: /docs/treasure-digital-master-plan.md
# ============================================================

## 1. IDENTITY & CONTEXT
- Company: "Treasure Digital" — a digital agency (App Dev, Web Dev, Digital Marketing,
  eShop/eCommerce, SEO, Google Ads, Meta/Facebook Ads, Social Media Management).
- Priority services (give visual weight): App Development, Web Development, Digital Marketing.
- Markets: Bulgaria (primary) + international. The site is the company's own portfolio —
  it must look like a top-tier agency at every screen size.
- Brand mark: an infinity loop in blue + amber with a digital "pixel-splash" detail.
  Meaning: endless growth, continuity, momentum.

## 2. TECH STACK (do not introduce alternatives without asking)
- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS (tokens below)
- next-intl (i18n), next-themes (dark/light)
- motion (Framer Motion; import from "motion/react")
- react-hook-form + zod (forms), resend (email)
- Sanity (next-sanity) for the blog
- lucide-react (icons), clsx + tailwind-merge (a `cn()` util)
- Hosting: Vercel. Rendering: SSG for all marketing pages.

## 3. HARD RULES (non-negotiable)
- NEVER hardcode hex colors in components. Use the CSS variables / Tailwind tokens only.
- NEVER use carousels, sliders, or auto-rotating hero banners. One static hero, one primary CTA.
- NEVER hardcode user-facing text in components — all copy comes from next-intl messages
  (src/messages/bg.json, src/messages/en.json). Bulgarian is the default; never ship English-only text.
- NEVER justify body text. Left-align, ~60–75 characters per line.
- NEVER use localStorage/sessionStorage for theme/state in SSR-rendered code — use cookies or next-themes.
- NEVER use native <form> submit behavior — handle via onSubmit handlers.
- Fonts MUST support Cyrillic. If a font lacks Cyrillic, do not use it.
- Currency is EURO (€) ONLY. There is no "лв."/leva anywhere. Use "от €X" (BG) / "from €X" (EN).
- Dark mode is the PRIMARY/default experience. Always ship a working light/dark toggle.

## 4. DESIGN TOKENS
Brand colors (sampled from official logo): blue #0061FE, amber #E8A50B, night #000817,
ink #1F1F1E, white #FFFFFF. Signature gradient (accents/glow ONLY):
  linear-gradient(120deg, #0061FE 0%, #2E7BFF 45%, #E8A50B 100%)

Use these CSS variables (defined in globals.css) via Tailwind tokens — never raw hex:
  bg, surface, surface-2, text, text-muted, border, primary, primary-foreground, accent, ring

Light mode:  bg #FFFFFF · surface #F5F7FA · surface-2 #ECEFF5 · text #1F1F1E ·
             text-muted #5B6472 · border #E5E8EF · primary #0061FE · accent #E8A50B
Dark mode:   bg #000817 · surface #0A1426 · surface-2 #12203A · text #FFFFFF ·
             text-muted #9AA7BD · border rgba(255,255,255,.08) ·
             primary #2E7BFF · accent #F5B028   (brightened for AA contrast on dark)

Both modes MUST pass WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1 body text). Use amber as a sparing accent (dots,
highlights, gradient end), not as a fill color for large areas.

## 5. TYPOGRAPHY
- Max TWO font families: one display (bold, geometric, Cyrillic-ready) + one body (clean, Cyrillic-ready).
- Load as variable fonts, font-display: swap, preload the above-the-fold display font.
- Type-first design: headlines are large and confident. Fluid sizing with clamp().
  Display XL clamp(2.75rem,6vw,5.5rem) · H1 clamp(2.25rem,4vw,3.5rem) ·
  H2 clamp(1.75rem,3vw,2.5rem) · H3 1.5rem · Body 1.0625rem/1.7 · Small 0.9375rem.

## 6. LAYOUT, SPACING, COMPONENTS
- Spacing scale: 4/8/12/16/24/32/48/64/96 px. Be generous — whitespace reads as premium.
- Radius: cards 1rem, large panels 1.5rem, buttons 0.75rem, pills full.
- Elevation in dark mode: subtle borders + soft blue/amber glows, not heavy black shadows.
- Use BENTO grids (mixed-size cards) for services and portfolio.
- Cards: bg-surface + border + rounded-2xl + hover lift + faint gradient edge.
- Buttons:
  - Primary: bg-primary, text-primary-foreground, radius .75rem; hover = darker blue + slight
    lift + glow 0 0 24px rgba(0,97,254,.4).
  - Secondary: transparent, border-border, text = --text; hover = border-primary.
- Header: sticky, translucent (backdrop-blur), dark-mode logo, nav, PERSISTENT primary CTA,
  theme toggle, BG/EN switcher.
- Echo the amber dots from the logo as small decorative markers (section numbers, list bullets).

## 7. MOTION
- Subtle and branded. Durations 150–400ms, ease cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1).
- Allowed: scroll-reveal, hover lift, animated stat counters, kinetic hero type, the infinity
  mark drawing itself (SVG stroke-dashoffset).
- Kinetic/animated type in the hero ONLY — never in body copy or navigation.
- Always respect prefers-reduced-motion.

## 8. INTERNATIONALIZATION
- Locales: ["bg","en"], defaultLocale "bg", localePrefix "as-needed"
  (Bulgarian at "/", English at "/en/").
- All routes under src/app/[locale]/. Add hreflang alternates in metadata.
- Slugs use Latin transliteration (e.g. /uslugi/web-razrabotka), not Cyrillic URLs.

## 9. SEO
- Unique <title> + meta description per page via generateMetadata (BG + EN).
- JSON-LD: Organization + LocalBusiness in root layout; Service + FAQPage on service pages;
  Article on blog posts; BreadcrumbList on inner pages.
- sitemap.ts (all locales/pages) + robots.ts that ALLOWS all crawlers and links the sitemap.
- Templated OG/Twitter images (1200×630, dark bg + gradient + logo).
- Every service is its own indexable page targeting one keyword cluster.

## 10. PERFORMANCE
- next/image for every image (WebP/AVIF, correct sizing, lazy-load below the fold).
- Targets: LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1, INP < 200ms.
- Minimal client JS; prefer Server Components; mark "use client" only when needed.
- Any background video (rare): muted, looped, < 5MB.

## 11. ACCESSIBILITY
- Semantic HTML, logical heading order, descriptive alt text, labeled form fields,
  full keyboard navigation, visible focus states, AA contrast.

## 12. CODE CONVENTIONS
- TypeScript strict. Functional components. Named exports for components.
- Files: components in src/components/{layout,sections,ui,seo}; one component per file.
- Use the cn() helper (clsx + tailwind-merge) for conditional classes.
- Keep data (services, pricing, nav) in src/lib data files, not inline in JSX.
- No dead code, no unused deps, no `any` unless justified with a comment.
- Prefer composition and small components over large monoliths.

## 13. COPY & CONTENT
- Lead with the OUTCOME (more clients / повече клиенти), not the feature.
- Headlines are clear and literal, never clever/ambiguous.
- One primary call-to-action per view; repeat the CTA after major sections.
- Free "site/SEO audit" lead magnet drives email capture.

## 14. HOW TO WORK (behavior)
- Build ONE section/component per request; do not scaffold the whole site in one shot.
- After a change, briefly state what you did and what to test (BG+EN, dark+light, mobile).
- If a request conflicts with these rules, point it out and propose a compliant alternative
  instead of silently breaking the rule.
- When unsure about a design choice, re-read /docs/treasure-digital-master-plan.md before guessing.
- For version-specific setup (especially next-intl App Router config), follow the CURRENT official
  approach if it differs from older snippets — keep the structure/decisions, update the syntax.

## 15. NEVER DO
- No carousels/sliders. No hardcoded hex or hardcoded copy. No justified text.
- No leva/"лв." — euros only. No English-only or Bulgarian-only gaps.
- No low-contrast muted text on dark. No heavy unoptimized hero media.
- No localStorage in SSR code. No native form submits. No non-Cyrillic fonts for UI text.
